          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Oliver Cromwell</strong><br>\nOliver Cromwell was born on April 25, 1599, in Huntingdon, England, into a middle-class gentry family. He was educated at Sidney Sussex College, Cambridge, which was known for its Puritan sympathies. His early life was ordinary, and he later entered the Parliament of England as a representative for Huntingdon in 1628.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cromwell's Role in the English Civil War</strong><br>\nCromwell became a leader in the Parliamentary army against King Charles I during the English Civil War. He was a talented soldier and quickly rose through the ranks, becoming a general. His leadership was crucial in the defeat of the Royalist forces, earning him the respect and trust of his troops and fellow Parliamentarians.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The New Model Army and Cromwell</strong><br>\nCromwell helped to reorganize the Parliamentary forces into the New Model Army, which became an efficient and disciplined fighting force. This army was a major factor in the success of the Parliamentarians. Cromwell's influence grew because of his military successes and his strong personality.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
