            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Cromwell's Political Power</strong><br>\nAfter the execution of King Charles I in 1649, Cromwell became a member of the Rump Parliament, the government that replaced the monarchy. He helped abolish the traditional monarchy and the House of Lords, believing they were corrupt and ineffective institutions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cromwell as Lord Protector</strong><br>\nIn 1653, Cromwell was named Lord Protector of England, Scotland, and Ireland, effectively making him the ruler of these countries. His rule was marked by efforts to reform society and government. He sought to spread Protestantism and advance educational and social reforms.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Religious Tolerance and Policies</strong><br>\nDespite being a Puritan, Cromwell advocated for certain levels of religious freedom, promoting a policy of tolerance towards different Protestant sects. However, his regime was intolerant of Catholics, whom he considered a threat to the stability of the nation.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
